<p>Ukraine&#x27;s patrol police chief, Yevhen Zhukov, resigned after video showed two officers leaving the scene of a shooting in Kyiv on Saturday while gunfire was still ringing out, intensifying scrutiny of the police response. Authorities said the shooting killed at least six people and injured more than a dozen. They also suspended the two officers seen in the footage while investigators reviewed their actions. Zhukov said he stepped down because he believed it was the right decision after what he described as a serious failure by the patrol force, as officials opened an inquiry into the officers&#x27; conduct.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Footage detail: Reports said the two officers stood next to a person on the ground before running as gunshots rang out, a vivid detail that made the video especially damaging.</li><li>How the fallout was framed: SCMP called the episode a &#x27;shameful&#x27; police response, widening the focus beyond a single personnel lapse.</li><li>Attack uncertainty: SCMP said the shooter was an unknown gunman, showing that key questions about the attacker remained unresolved even as scrutiny centered on police behavior.</li></ul><blockquote>As an officer with combat experience, I have decided to tender my resignation from my current post. I believe this is the right thing to do. - Yevhen Zhukov</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Yevhen Zhukov: By invoking his combat experience when he stepped down, he framed the resignation as a leadership duty, suggesting commanders should answer for failures below them. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350652/police-patrol-chief-quits-over-shameful-response-kyiv-shooting'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Ukrainian authorities: Their response was both procedural and disciplinary, with suspensions followed by an inquiry that placed the video evidence at the center of the accountability process. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8ejn778j4do'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Euronews reporting: Its emphasis on officers &#x27;fleeing in panic&#x27; shifted attention from the gunman alone to a broader question of whether patrol officers were ready to respond under fire. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/19/two-police-officers-suspended-after-fleeing-kyiv-shooting-scene'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8ejn778j4do'>Ukraine police chief resigns after officers allegedly fled deadly shooting</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350652/police-patrol-chief-quits-over-shameful-response-kyiv-shooting'>Ukraine’s patrol chief quits over ‘shameful’ police response to deadly Kyiv shooting</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/19/two-police-officers-suspended-after-fleeing-kyiv-shooting-scene'>Two police officers suspended after fleeing Kyiv shooting scene</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/two-police-officers-suspended-over-claims-they-fled-kyiv-shooting'>Two officers suspended in Ukraine over claims they fled Kyiv shooting</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>